From 1bca7e1044aa267414e1200790ec4135c9623ad5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:00:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-40: the hand -- hold Space and drag (or a
 middle-button drag) to pan the view (0.40.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WPF / Blend: Space held turns the pointer into a hand and a drag pans the
design surface; a middle-button drag pans too. Handy once zoomed in.
- while Space is held a shield in the overlay covers the page (cursor grab /
  grabbing), so nothing below is hovered, picked, moved or clicked; the page
  never sees the Space (no page-down either); keyup / blur / operate mode
  end it; in an input or a contenteditable Space stays a space
- a middle-button drag on the page pans the same way (Chrome's autoscroll
  suppressed); the click / auxclick that ends a pan is swallowed
- the design-mode hint line mentions it

CHEATSHEET: the two property-panel rows added in R30 / R32 moved from
"移動、大小" to the 屬性面板 section; the pan row under 顯示.

Test: probe (zoom 200%: Space + drag of (-100, -50) scrolls to (100, 50),
the shield shown then hidden; a middle-button drag of -60 scrolls on --
up to the page's edge; no edit, no selection).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
